---
// CONCEPT — the iceberg, fully explained. Observation deck → source.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import LayerDescent from '../components/LayerDescent.astro'
import { ICEBERG_FLOW, TAGLINES } from '../data/ontology'
---

<BaseLayout title="The Iceberg — concept — PIL.AGRIGEA" description="The iceberg is an inference engine: 10% observable, 90% inferred.">
  <div class="container" style="padding-top: var(--space-7); padding-bottom: var(--space-7);">
    <p class="section__label"><a href="/">← The Deck</a></p>
    <h1>The Iceberg</h1>
    <p class="mono faint" style="letter-spacing:0.14em; margin-bottom: var(--space-6);">{ICEBERG_FLOW}</p>

    <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-7);">
      The iceberg is an <strong>inference engine</strong>. Ten percent of it is
      observable from the surface — the events, the data, the effects. Ninety
      percent of it is below the line: the patterns, the mechanisms, the
      paradigms that produce what we see. {TAGLINES.observation}
    </p>

    <section class="prose" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-7);">
      <h2>Why an iceberg?</h2>
      <p>
        Because the interesting part of any phenomenon is the part you cannot
        see. A stock crash is an effect — its cause lives a kilometer down, in
        the paradigm that allowed the leverage. An AI model's output is an
        effect — its cause lives in the training data, which is a culture.
        Standing on the observation line, you only ever see the tip. The
        descent is the method for seeing the rest.
      </p>
      <p>
        The layers are not levels of importance — they are levels of inference.
        <strong>MATRIX</strong> (0m) does not explain; it presents.{" "}
        <strong>FRAMES</strong> (−50m) detect patterns: taxonomies, timelines,
        maps. <strong>PILLS</strong> (−200m) infer mechanisms — and pills are
        hypotheses, never facts. <strong>DEEP</strong> (−500m) validates
        causality: consensus built or broken. <strong>SOURCE</strong> (−1000m)
        is the paradigm — bedrock. Ours is self-hosted infrastructure, trading
        algorithms, and the methodology itself.
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        "WE ARE COOKING KNOWLEDGE" — the source is the stove, the deck is the
        kitchen, and every fish is a dish still on the fire.
      </blockquote>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: var(--space-7);">
      <h2>The descent, layer by layer</h2>
      <LayerDescent />
    </section>

    <section class="prose" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-7);">
      <h2>The feedback loop</h2>
      <p>
        The flow is downward — observation to paradigm — but the influence is
        upward. A paradigm at −1000m shapes what the matrix at 0m can even
        observe. The deck is where the two meet: you stand at the surface,
        looking down the descent, watching the source steer the surface.
        {TAGLINES.ethos}
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="hero__cta">
      <a class="btn btn--active" href="/fishes/">SEE THE FISH</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/tree/">OR CLIMB THE TREE</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
